== Notes ==
* {{Dlc|r}} Unlike all other other alternative versions of bosses, such as {{e|Dangle}}, {{e|C.H.A.D.}}, and {{e|Gish}}, Triachnid has the same weight as his alternative boss form.
** Although they share the same weight, Triachnid is actually '''more''' common than {{e|Daddy Long Legs}}, since he also appears in the Scarred Womb.

== Trivia ==
* Triachnid was added in the ''Wrath of the Lamb'' DLC for the original ''The Binding of Isaac''.
** In the original game, Triachnid could be encountered in {{s|Necropolis}}.
** Triachnid's unlock method is possibly a reference to a bug in ''Wrath of the Lamb'' that caused Triachnid to occasionally replace {{e|Isaac}} in the {{s|Cathedral}}.
* Triachnid originated from the 2006 flash game ''[http://www.newgrounds.com/portal/view/347467 Tri-achnid]'', which was created by Edmund McMillen.
* He is an alternative of {{e|Daddy Long Legs}}.
** Unlike the other alternate bosses ({{e|Steven}}, {{E|C.H.A.D.}}, {{E|Gish}}, and {{e|Conquest}}), Triachnid does not drop a specific item.
* While Daddy Long Legs uses 4 appendages in his attacks, Triachnid is reduced to mostly only using 3; this is most likely in homage to the fact that Triachnid in his title game only had 3 appendages.
* {{dlc|na+}} Triachnid does not have a death animation.
* {{dlc+|a+}} Triachnid can be found in {{s|The Void}}, even before being unlocked.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc|r}} {{e|Blighted Ovum}}, {{e|Big Horn}}, Triachnid, Isaac, and {{e|???}} are the only bosses whose portraits were completely changed in ''Repentance'' (beyond simply adding more detail). Of these, only Triachnid, Isaac, and ??? didn't receive new sprites.

